      "message": "Between the two I prefer Himanshu alternative,\nI think it is a bit cleaner (the -2 in David proposition is really weird)\n\nI would even tweak it a bit to not break and to make it obvious that the 0 is returned when there is no scn available\n\n\n```suggestion\n  uint8_t idx \u003d btm_cb.scn_last_idx;\n  do {\n    idx++;\n    if (idx \u003e\u003d PORT_MAX_RFC_PORTS) {\n      idx \u003d 1; // Index 0 is reserved for hfp\n    }\n  } while (idx !\u003d btm_cb.btm_available_index \u0026\u0026 btm_cb.btm_scn[idx]);\n  \n  if (btm_cb.btm_scn[idx]) {\n      return 0; // No scn available\n  }\n  \n  btm_cb.btm_scn[idx] \u003d true;\n  btm_cb.scn_last_idx \u003d idx;\n  return (idx + 1); // +1 to move from an array base index to a number\n```\n\nthe `do ... while` can also be a for loop, but somehow i find it confusing\n```\n  for (idx \u003d btm_cb.scn_last_idx + 1;\n       idx !\u003d btm_cb.btm_available_index \u0026\u0026 btm_cb.btm_scn[idx];\n       ++idx) {\n    if (idx \u003e\u003d PORT_MAX_RFC_PORTS) {\n      idx \u003d 1; // Index 0 is reserved for hfp\n    }\n  }\n```",
